TQue Buffer Limit
The buffer allocated by the TQue stores the synchronization event ID. Therefore,
the number of QUE buffers in the same TPosition is related to the synchronization
event ID of the hardware.
For the Atlas Training Series Product, the number of event IDs is 4.
The maximum number of buffers of the QUE is 8 or 4, that is, the number of
synchronization events that can be inserted is 8 or 4. When the InitBuffer of the
TPipe is used to allocate TQue, the maximum number of TQue that can be
allocated is 8 or 4 due to buffer limits.
If the number of QUE buffers used at the same time exceeds the limit, no more
TQue can be allocated.

